// Base bullion (OreProcessing, #740): what any form of a by-product ore smelts to, a bar of 100 units of
// the ore's main metal still carrying its by-product, which only a parting machine wins (Ore/Core/Bullion.cs).
// Silver-lead (galena, argentiferous galena), argentiferous copper (tetrahedrite), cupriferous silver
// (freibergite), tin-lead (teallite, franckeite) and doré (gold quartz). The metal is the code's last part:
// the crucible and the ingot mold draw it by that. Smelted plainly it gives its main metal (set in code).
// partedBy names the machine that parts each kind (the config's byProducts.partedBy, held to it by
// BullionTests), for the tooltip's one line (ItemOreProduct.StatusText). Marked disabled with the switch off.
// Drawn as the game's ingot, with its transforms, tongs and shelf (game:itemtypes/resource/ingot.json); doré
// in the shiny ingot and pile, as the game's gold (both shapes take the one "metal" texture, so the blended
// overlays hold). The dimensions stay: the crucible fits a bar by them. Not worked on the anvil. Each kind's
// handbook page is its own (groupBy by ore, so Tidy Variants keeps them apart too), its "Ore processing"
// section its own text (extraSectionsByType; the figures generated, Ore/tools/make_ore_guide_numbers.py),
// linking the guide "Base bullion" (config/handbook/oreprocessing-bullion.json).
